{
    "background_story": "Avah was a young weaver from Tabriz, a city in northwest Iran famous for its rich history and exquisite carpets. Growing up, she learned the ancient art of weaving from her mother and grandmother, who had passed down the techniques through generations. Avah's fingers moved deftly as she wove intricate patterns and designs onto the loom, creating stunning works of art that told stories of her city's heritage. Her carpets were highly sought after by merchants and travelers, who would take them to far-off lands, spreading the beauty and craftsmanship of Tabriz. Avah's passion for weaving was not just about creating something beautiful, but also about preserving the traditions and history of her beloved city. She became known as one of the finest weavers in Tabriz, and her carpets remain a testament to the city's enduring legacy.",
